WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.977
How does every machine in a growing cluster know which other machines are still alive, without the amount of network chatter exploding as the cluster grows?

00:00:09.977 --> 00:00:15.412
This is SWIM, the gossip protocol behind failure detection in Gimle's service fabric.

00:00:16.312 --> 00:00:19.448
Every node runs on a steady one second cycle.

00:00:19.448 --> 00:00:23.559
Each tick, it picks one other member and pings it directly.

00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:30.457
If an acknowledgement comes back in time, that member is confirmed alive, and nothing else happens.

00:00:31.357 --> 00:00:35.854
But this time, Node B doesn't answer within its ping timeout.

00:00:35.854 --> 00:00:38.729
That alone doesn't mean Node B is down.

00:00:38.729 --> 00:00:44.258
It could just as easily be a bad network path between only these two nodes.

00:00:45.158 --> 00:00:55.234
So instead of giving up, Node A asks a handful of other members, here Node C and Node D, to relay probe Node B on its behalf.

00:00:55.234 --> 00:01:01.279
Each of them sends its own direct ping to B and reports back what it finds.

00:01:02.179 --> 00:01:11.186
Only when the direct probe and every indirect relay all fail does Node A mark Node B as suspect, not dead yet, just suspect.

00:01:12.086 --> 00:01:16.356
A suspected node gets a real chance to prove it's still there.

00:01:16.356 --> 00:01:24.415
If Node B were actually fine, just briefly overloaded, it could refute the suspicion at any point during this window.

00:01:24.415 --> 00:01:32.267
Only once the suspicion timeout, about three seconds, elapses with no refutation does Node A finally mark it dead.

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:36.041
That new status doesn't need a broadcast.

00:01:36.041 --> 00:01:47.256
It piggybacks on whatever ordinary gossip traffic Node A was already sending, spreading through the cluster the way a rumor spreads through casual conversation.

00:01:47.256 --> 00:01:54.265
And every 30 seconds, a full anti entropy sync acts as a backstop, in case any node missed the news.

00:01:55.165 --> 00:02:01.834
That's direct pings, indirect probes, suspicion, and gossip dissemination, the core of SWIM.

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:14.300
The full concepts page covers the local health multiplier that adapts these timeouts under load, and why this same mechanism is what actually triggers Gimle's self-healing.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.532
Link in the docs.

